  "lineage": "Pimba is the Portuguese popular song of village arraiais, summer festivals and emigrant gatherings, a name popularised in the 1990s by the refrain of Emanuel's song 'Pimba, Pimba' and applied to singalong songs full of double meanings and dance rhythms drawn from the marcha, the vira and modern pop. Its records usually set a solo singer over keyboards, drums, electric bass, guitar and accordion, and it is studied as working-class popular music by researchers at INET-md.",
